OpenLDAP on openRuyi
===================

Defaults
--------
slapd runs as ldap and listens only on ldapi:///.
Local root can manage cn=config through SASL EXTERNAL.
The initial configuration contains no default password or user directory database.

For existing OpenLDAP 2.6 databases, follow the migration section below.

Initialize a new installation
-----------------------------
Install openldap-client. Stop slapd. Run these commands as root only for a new installation:

    mkdir -m 0700 /etc/openldap/slapd.d &&
    slapadd -F /etc/openldap/slapd.d -n 0 -l @DATADIR@/openldap/slapd-initial.ldif &&
    slaptest -F /etc/openldap/slapd.d -u &&
    chown -R ldap:ldap /etc/openldap/slapd.d

If a command fails, keep the directory and leave slapd stopped.
Do not delete existing configuration to repeat initialization.
After all commands succeed:

    systemctl start slapd
    ldapsearch -Q -Y EXTERNAL -H ldapi:/// -b cn=config dn

Service configuration
---------------------
Use systemctl edit slapd to override ExecStart and change listeners or process options.
Clear ExecStart with an empty assignment before setting its replacement.
The service does not read /etc/sysconfig/openldap or use slapd.conf by default.
ProtectHome=true blocks service access to home directories.
Store TLS files elsewhere and give ldap read access.
For TCP ports that require privileges, grant the service CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE.
Configure TLS and access controls before enabling network access.

OpenLDAP 2.6 databases
---------------------
OpenLDAP 2.7 uses a different MDB format. The package does not migrate data.

Stop slapd. Keep the original data unchanged.
If you have no LDIF export, use a working 2.6 environment.
Export a copy of the old database with the 2.6 slapcat.
Use the 2.7 slapadd to import the LDIF into a new directory.
Follow the migration instructions before starting slapd:

https://www.openldap.org/doc/admin27/appendix-upgrading.html

Database, schema and TLS configuration:
https://www.openldap.org/doc/admin27/
